      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T11:24:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we extend this handling to `print_array()`? Scalar array elements still use typed pointers directly. For example, `pipe_create_reply.pipe_sw_if_index[2]` starts at offset 14, so generated `fromjson` passes a 2-mod-4 address to a helper that writes through `u32 *`. This retains the strict-alignment/UBSan failure this change is intended to fix. Please cover fixed and variable-length scalar arrays through aligned temporaries or a common unaligned accessor.",
      "revId": "5abbee4aaac9627b9cd57c53f7508e52ef77c5fa",
