      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T11:24:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This `(void *)` cast is emitted for aggregates as well as scalars, but aggregate formatters still retrieve `vl_api_\u003ctype\u003e_t *` with `va_arg`. Passing `void *` and retrieving an aggregate pointer is an incompatible variadic argument pair and therefore undefined behavior. For example, generated calls to `format_vl_api_address_t` now pass `void *`, while that formatter expects `vl_api_address_t *`. Please keep aggregate arguments typed and use `void *` only with formatters whose contract explicitly requires it. The array path below has the same issue.",
      "revId": "5abbee4aaac9627b9cd57c53f7508e52ef77c5fa",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
