      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T11:24:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This changes the public generated C API: scalar endian and calc-size helpers change from `vl_api_\u003ctype\u003e_t *` to `void *`, and scalar formatters change their variadic argument contract. Out-of-tree consumers using typed function pointers can fail to compile, while existing formatter calls can continue compiling but invoke undefined behavior.\n\nThe packed wire format itself remains unchanged; the compatibility break is in the generated C interface. Could we preserve the existing public helpers and introduce internal unaligned accessors for generated packed-message call sites instead? An alignment-one typedef following VPP\u0027s existing `u32u` pattern may also preserve the signatures, but changing `_Alignof(vl_api_\u003ctype\u003e_t)` could alter consumer-defined structure layouts and would need a compatibility assessment.",
      "revId": "5abbee4aaac9627b9cd57c53f7508e52ef77c5fa",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
